    <item>
      <title>Tab bar</title>
      <link>https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/tab-bar/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/tab-bar/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Little Go&amp;rsquo;s user interface consists of several distinct areas. A tab bar lets you navigate between those areas. Only one area can be visible at any given time.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-toc gdoc-toc__level--6&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;nav id=&#34;TableOfContents&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#different-tab-bars-for-iphone-and-ipad&#34;&gt;Different tab bars for iPhone and iPad&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;      &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;        &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#iphone-devices&#34;&gt;iPhone devices&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;        &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#ipad-devices-ios-17-or-older&#34;&gt;iPad devices, iOS 17 or older&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;        &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#ipad-devices-ios-18-or-newer&#34;&gt;iPad devices, iOS 18 or newer&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#list-of-ui-areas&#34;&gt;List of UI areas&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#how-to-edit-the-tab-bar&#34;&gt;How to edit the tab bar&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/nav&gt;&#xA;      &lt;hr /&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h2 id=&#34;different-tab-bars-for-iphone-and-ipad&#34;&#xA;    &gt;&#xA;        Different tab bars for iPhone and iPad&#xA;    &lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;    &lt;a data-clipboard-text=&#34;https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/tab-bar/#different-tab-bars-for-iphone-and-ipad&#34; class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center&#34; title=&#34;Anchor to: Different tab bars for iPhone and iPad&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor to: Different tab bars for iPhone and iPad&#34; href=&#34;#different-tab-bars-for-iphone-and-ipad&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The app tries to minimize the differences between the iPhone and iPad user interfaces, and where there are small differences this user manual usually does not specifically point them out. In the case of the tab bar, however, the differences are too big to be ignored.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Toolbar in the Play area</title>
      <link>https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-toolbar/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-toolbar/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;The Play &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt; user interface area displays a toolbar with buttons that perform various actions. An overview of the general toolbar organization is given in the next section, while the section after that provides a reference of all the buttons that can appear in the toolbar, and what they do.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-toc gdoc-toc__level--6&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;nav id=&#34;TableOfContents&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#toolbar-organization&#34;&gt;Toolbar organization&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#button-reference&#34;&gt;Button reference&lt;/a&gt;&#xA;      &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;        &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#right-toolbar-area&#34;&gt;Right toolbar area&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;        &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#play-mode&#34;&gt;Play mode&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;        &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#scoring-mode&#34;&gt;Scoring mode&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;        &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#board-setup-mode&#34;&gt;Board setup mode&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;        &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#markup-editing-mode&#34;&gt;Markup editing mode&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/li&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/nav&gt;&#xA;      &lt;hr /&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h2 id=&#34;toolbar-organization&#34;&#xA;    &gt;&#xA;        Toolbar organization&#xA;    &lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;    &lt;a data-clipboard-text=&#34;https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-toolbar/#toolbar-organization&#34; class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center&#34; title=&#34;Anchor to: Toolbar organization&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor to: Toolbar organization&#34; href=&#34;#toolbar-organization&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This is how the Play &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt; area toolbar looks like on an iPhone when you hold the device in portrait orientation. On the iPad the toolbar is wider but in general has the same content.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Menu in the Play area</title>
      <link>https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-menu/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-menu/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;In the Play &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt; area when you tap the Menu &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon menu-hamburger&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#menu-hamburger&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt; button a menu will pop up that looks similar to the following screenshot:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-columns gdoc-columns--small flex gap-16 flex-mobile-column&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-columns__content gdoc-markdown--nested flex-even&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;div class=&#34;flex justify-center&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;figure class=&#34;gdoc-markdown__figure&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;a class=&#34;gdoc-markdown__link--raw&#34; href=&#34;https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-menu/play-menu.jpg&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;picture&gt;&#xA;          &lt;img&#xA;                src=&#34;https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-menu/play-menu.jpg&#34;&#xA;              alt=&#34;Menu Play area (iPhone)&#34;&#xA;          /&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/picture&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;        &lt;figcaption&gt;&#xA;          Menu Play area (iPhone)&#xA;        &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-columns__content gdoc-markdown--nested flex-even&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;p&gt;Menu items are actions for which there is no toolbar button. The mode that is currently active in the Play &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt; area affects which items the menu shows. See &lt;a&#xA;  class=&#34;gdoc-markdown__link&#34;&#xA;  href=&#34;https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-area-modes/&#34;&#xA;&gt;this page&lt;/a&gt; for more information on Play &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt; area modes.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Status Text in the Play area</title>
      <link>https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-status-text/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-status-text/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;On the Play &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt; area there is always a view that shows context-related textual information about what is currently going on in the game. This textual information is called the Status Text.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-toc gdoc-toc__level--6&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;nav id=&#34;TableOfContents&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;ul&gt;&#xA;    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#locaton-on-the-screen&#34;&gt;Locaton on the screen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#play-mode&#34;&gt;Play mode&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#scoring-mode&#34;&gt;Scoring mode&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#board-setup-mode&#34;&gt;Board setup mode&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#markup-editing-mode&#34;&gt;Markup editing mode&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;#when-computer-is-calculating&#34;&gt;When computer is calculating&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;/nav&gt;&#xA;      &lt;hr /&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h2 id=&#34;locaton-on-the-screen&#34;&#xA;    &gt;&#xA;        Locaton on the screen&#xA;    &lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;    &lt;a data-clipboard-text=&#34;https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-status-text/#locaton-on-the-screen&#34; class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center&#34; title=&#34;Anchor to: Locaton on the screen&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor to: Locaton on the screen&#34; href=&#34;#locaton-on-the-screen&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-columns gdoc-columns--small flex gap-16 flex-mobile-column&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-columns__content gdoc-markdown--nested flex-even&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;div class=&#34;flex justify-center&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;figure class=&#34;gdoc-markdown__figure&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;a class=&#34;gdoc-markdown__link--raw&#34; href=&#34;https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-status-text/play-status-text-portrait.svg&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;picture&gt;&#xA;          &lt;img&#xA;              src=&#34;https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-status-text/play-status-text-portrait.svg&#34; width=&#34;&#34;&#xA;          /&gt;&#xA;        &lt;/picture&gt;&#xA;      &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;        &lt;figcaption&gt;&#xA;          Status Text location in portrait orientation&#xA;        &lt;/figcaption&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/figure&gt;&#xA;  &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;    &lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-columns__content gdoc-markdown--nested flex-even&#34;&gt;&#xA;      The user interface always shows the Status Text in the same location, independent of the device orientation: Near the top of the screen, right above the game board.&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h2 id=&#34;play-mode&#34;&#xA;    &gt;&#xA;        Play mode&#xA;    &lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;    &lt;a data-clipboard-text=&#34;https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-status-text/#play-mode&#34; class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center&#34; title=&#34;Anchor to: Play mode&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor to: Play mode&#34; href=&#34;#play-mode&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The Status Text shows the following information when Play &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt; mode is active.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Modes in the Play area</title>
      <link>https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-area-modes/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-area-modes/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;At any given time the Play &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt; area of the user interface is in a specific state, or mode. The mode that is currently active affects all aspects of the Play &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt; area user interface:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The gestures that are available to interact with the board.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The symbols that are shown on the board.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The buttons that are shown in &lt;a&#xA;  class=&#34;gdoc-markdown__link&#34;&#xA;  href=&#34;https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-toolbar/&#34;&#xA;&gt;the toolbar&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The entries that appear in &lt;a&#xA;  class=&#34;gdoc-markdown__link&#34;&#xA;  href=&#34;https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-menu/&#34;&#xA;&gt;the menu&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;The information that &lt;a&#xA;  class=&#34;gdoc-markdown__link&#34;&#xA;  href=&#34;https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-status-text/&#34;&#xA;&gt;the Status Text&lt;/a&gt; displays.&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;flex align-center gdoc-page__anchorwrap&#34;&gt;&#xA;    &lt;h2 id=&#34;play-mode&#34;&#xA;    &gt;&#xA;        Play mode&#xA;    &lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;    &lt;a data-clipboard-text=&#34;https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/play-area-modes/#play-mode&#34; class=&#34;gdoc-page__anchor clip flex align-center&#34; title=&#34;Anchor to: Play mode&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor to: Play mode&#34; href=&#34;#play-mode&#34;&gt;&#xA;        &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gdoc_link&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/a&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When Play &lt;svg class=&#34;gdoc-icon gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;use xlink:href=&#34;#gogrid2x2&#34;&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt; mode is active the user interface provides interactions geared towards playing the game. You can place a stone or play a pass move, let the computer play a move on your behalf, pause/continue the game in a computer vs. computer game, and so on.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Landscape orientation</title>
      <link>https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/landscape/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/ui-basics/landscape/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Below you can see how the user interface looks like on an iPhone device, both in portrait and in landscape orientation.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;To make optimal use of the available space the areas of the user interface are shifted around when the orientation changes. The annotation numbers in the illustration show where each area goes when the user interface orientation changes from portrait to landscape, and vice versa.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;blockquote class=&#34;gdoc-hint note&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-hint__title flex gap-8 align-center&#34;&gt;&lt;i class=&#34;fa note&#34;&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&#xA;      &lt;span&gt;Note&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;gdoc-hint__text&#34;&gt;On iPad devices the basic layout is the same as on iPhone devices. The only difference is the amount of space that is available to each user interface element.&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a&#xA;  class=&#34;gdoc-markdown__link&#34;&#xA;  href=&#34;https://littlego-usermanual.herzbube.ch/&#34;&#xA;&gt;main page&lt;/a&gt; of this user manual has more information on the meaning of each of the numbered UI areas.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
